IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cards-domain`
IMPORT `earn-kernel`
IMPORT `citi-exclusions`
IMPORT fixtures

§ `Citibank PremierMiles Program Terms and Conditions`

-- ===========================================================================
-- DOCUMENT. citi-premiermiles-agreement: the Citibank PremierMiles
-- Visa/Mastercard Cardmember's Agreement, whose last section is the "Citibank
-- PremierMiles Program Terms and Conditions" cl.1-5. "Printed on Feb 2025.
-- With effect from 1 May 2025." (Citibank Singapore Limited). The earn terms
-- are cl.3, so this module encodes cl.3 (and cl.2 where it bears on who
-- earns); the rest of the 27-page agreement is the credit facility, which is
-- out of scope.
--
-- THIS AGREEMENT DOES STATE EARN RATES: cl.3.1 states them. (The earlier
-- encoding row of this subject held no PremierMiles terms.)
--
-- WHAT THE TEXT SAYS.
--   cl.3.1 1.2 Citi Miles for every S$1 of LOCAL retail purchases (a retail
--          purchase "denominated in S$", cl.1.1) and 2.2 Citi Miles for every
--          S$1 of OVERSEAS retail purchases ("denominated in a currency other
--          than S$"). Supplementary cardmembers' purchases are aggregated for
--          the basic cardmember; supplementary cardmembers earn nothing.
--   cl.3.2 Miles are calculated on the amount of EACH retail purchase
--          transaction and "rounded down to the nearest Citi Mile". A
--          refunded purchase earns nothing and a credited mile is debited.
--   cl.3.3 Twelve classes of transaction earn nothing, including (xii) the
--          Citi exclusion list by reference.
--   cl.3.4 10,000 Citi Miles (or another number the Bank determines) on
--          renewal of the annual membership, provided purchases were charged
--          in that membership year.
--   cl.3.6 Citi Miles do not expire.
-- NO CAP, NO HURDLE, NO CATEGORY: one flat rate each way.
--
-- THE FORK F-pm-visa. The agreement is for the "Visa/Mastercard" card and says
-- nothing of a withdrawal of the Visa; a Mainly Miles article (not read in full)
-- reports the Visa was retired at the start of 2026. Both networks earn the
-- same under cl.3.1, so no rate depends on it.
--
-- THE CARD-ON-FILE AND WALLET FACTS DO NOT MATTER HERE. cl.3 does not read how
-- the card was presented or what the merchant flagged. Local/overseas turns on
-- the currency of the charge alone.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `cl.3.1 -- the two flat rates`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Citi Miles per S$1 of local retail purchases` MEANS 1.2

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Citi Miles per S$1 of overseas retail purchases` MEANS 2.2

-- cl.1.1: "local retail purchase" means one "denominated in S$"; "overseas retail
-- purchase" means one "denominated in a currency other than S$".
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is denominated in Singapore dollars` p MEANS
    p's currency EQUALS `Singapore dollars`

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the PremierMiles rate on` p MEANS
    IF `the purchase is denominated in Singapore dollars` p
    THEN `Citi Miles per S$1 of local retail purchases`
    ELSE `Citi Miles per S$1 of overseas retail purchases`


§§ `cl.3.3 -- what earns nothing`

-- cl.3.3(i)-(xi) by kind of charge. (i) annual fees, interest, late payment
-- charges, GST, cash advances, instalment/easy/extended/equal payment plans,
-- preferred payment plans, balance transfers, quasi-cash, all fees; (ii) funds
-- transfers using the card as source of funds; (iii) bill payments "(including
-- via Citibank Online or via any other channel or agent)" -- a `Bill payment`
-- through a bank or agent channel is excluded; a bill paid directly to the biller
-- on the card is the open reading (fork F-bill-payments), floor 0, ceiling the full earn; (x) any
-- top-ups or payment of funds to payment service providers, prepaid cards and
-- prepaid accounts; (xi) transit-related transactions. Education (iv),
-- government (v), insurance (vi), financial institutions (vii), non-profit
-- organisations (viii) and betting (ix) are classes of PAYEE: they are caught
-- by the Citi exclusion list's merchant category codes (cl.3.3(xii)), which the
-- module reads from citi-exclusions.l4.
GIVEN k IS A `Charge kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`PremierMiles cl.3.3 excludes the kind` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `Retail purchase`                                   THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Bill payment`                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Top-up of a prepaid card or stored-value account`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Payment of funds to a payment service provider`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Instalment plan charge`                            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `My Preferred Payment Plan charge`                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Cash advance`                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Balance transfer or funds transfer`                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Fee, interest or finance charge`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Pre-authorisation`                                 THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Payment through UOB Payment Facility`              THEN FALSE
    WHEN `NETS or NETS-related transaction`                  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `SmartPay or personal loan`                         THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Transit-related transaction`                       THEN TRUE

-- cl.3.2: a refunded purchase is not accredited.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`PremierMiles excludes the purchase` p MEANS
    `PremierMiles cl.3.3 excludes the kind` (p's `charge kind`)
    OR `the Citi exclusion list excludes` p
    OR p's `later reversed`


§§ `cl.3.2 -- the miles a purchase earns, to the nearest mile down`

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Citi Miles on` p MEANS
    `rounded down to a whole number` ((p's `amount in SGD`) TIMES (`the PremierMiles rate on` p))

-- The earn on one purchase whose code is settled (known, or stood in).
GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`PremierMiles earn when the code is settled` c p MEANS
    IF `PremierMiles excludes the purchase` p
    THEN `nothing is earned on` c `in` `Citi Miles` `per` "Citibank PremierMiles Program T&C cl.3.3"
    ELSE `an answer for` c `in` `Citi Miles` `of` (`the Citi Miles on` p) `to` (`the Citi Miles on` p) `wanting` 0 `at` (JUST 1) `excluded` FALSE `drawing on` `No pot` `depending on` EMPTY `per` "Citibank PremierMiles Program T&C cl.3.1-3.2"

-- Codes for the worst-case and best-case evaluations: 6529 is on the Citi
-- list, 5999 is not.
`a code the Citi list excludes` MEANS 6529
`a code the Citi list does not exclude` MEANS 5999

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`PremierMiles earn at the worst code` c p MEANS
    `PremierMiles earn when the code is settled` c (`recoded purchase` p `a code the Citi list excludes`)

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`PremierMiles earn at the best code` c p MEANS
    `PremierMiles earn when the code is settled` c (`recoded purchase` p `a code the Citi list does not exclude`)

GIVEN c IS A Card
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`PremierMiles earns nothing under the open reading` c MEANS
    `nothing is earned on` c `in` `Citi Miles` `per` "Citi exclusion list cl.2 heading ranges"

-- The earn on a purchase. Two open questions bracket it: the code is not
-- known; only Reading 2 of the exclusion list's ranges would exclude it.
GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Citi PremierMiles earns on` c p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the code is unknown for` p
            THEN `bracketed from` (`PremierMiles earn at the worst code` c p) `to` (`PremierMiles earn at the best code` c p) `adding` (LIST `The merchant category code is not known`)
        IF p's `charge kind` EQUALS `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`
            THEN `bracketed from` (`PremierMiles earns nothing under the open reading` c) `to` (`PremierMiles earn when the code is settled` c p) `adding` (LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`)
        IF `only the Citi ranges would exclude` p
            THEN `bracketed from` (`PremierMiles earns nothing under the open reading` c) `to` (`PremierMiles earn when the code is settled` c p) `adding` (LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`)
        OTHERWISE `PremierMiles earn when the code is settled` c p


§§ `cl.3.4 -- the renewal bonus`

-- "10,000 Citi Miles (or such other number of Citi Miles as the Bank may from
-- time to time determine)" on renewal of the annual membership, provided
-- retail purchases were charged in that membership year.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Citi Miles on renewal of the annual membership` MEANS 10000

GIVEN purchasesChargedThisMembershipYear IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the renewal Citi Miles for` purchasesChargedThisMembershipYear MEANS
    IF purchasesChargedThisMembershipYear THEN `Citi Miles on renewal of the annual membership` ELSE 0


§§ `Illustrations -- built from cl.3.1 and cl.3.2`

`a PremierMiles card` MEANS `Citi PremierMiles Mastercard`

-- Named scenarios. Each differs from the base purchase (S$100, MCC 5812, in
-- Singapore dollars) in the fields its name says.
`S$100 in Singapore dollars` MEANS `the base purchase`
`S$100 in Malaysian ringgit` MEANS `purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Malaysian ringgit`
`S$100 in another foreign currency` MEANS `purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Another foreign currency`
`S$4.80 in Singapore dollars` MEANS `purchase for` `the base purchase` 4.80
`S$99.99 in Singapore dollars` MEANS `purchase for` `the base purchase` 99.99
`S$0.80 in Singapore dollars` MEANS `purchase for` `the base purchase` 0.80
`S$10.45 in Thai baht` MEANS `purchase in currency` (`purchase for` `the base purchase` 10.45) `Thai baht`
`S$100 at a store overseas but charged in S$` MEANS `purchase at location` `the base purchase` `A store outside Singapore`

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`PremierMiles on` p MEANS `Citi PremierMiles earns on` `a PremierMiles card` p

-- cl.3.1: S$100 local earns 120, S$100 overseas earns 220.
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` `S$100 in Singapore dollars`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` `S$100 in Singapore dollars`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` `S$100 in Malaysian ringgit`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 220
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` `S$100 in another foreign currency`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 220

-- cl.3.2: rounded down per transaction. S$4.80 x 1.2 = 5.76 -> 5; S$99.99 x 1.2 =
-- 119.988 -> 119; S$10.45 overseas x 2.2 = 22.99 -> 22; S$0.80 x 1.2 = 0.96 -> 0.
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` `S$4.80 in Singapore dollars`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` `S$99.99 in Singapore dollars`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 119
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` `S$10.45 in Thai baht`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 22
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` `S$0.80 in Singapore dollars`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 0

-- cl.1.1: denominated, not made: a purchase made overseas but charged in S$ is local.
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` `S$100 at a store overseas but charged in S$`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 120

-- cl.3.3(iii): a bill paid directly to the biller on the card is the open reading.
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`))'s `units at best` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT elem `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)` ((`PremierMiles on` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`))'s `depends on`)

-- cl.3.3: nothing earned on a bill payment, an instalment charge, a cash advance,
-- a top-up, a transit-related charge, a fee or a funds transfer.
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Bill payment`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Instalment plan charge`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `My Preferred Payment Plan charge`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Cash advance`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Top-up of a prepaid card or stored-value account`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Payment of funds to a payment service provider`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Transit-related transaction`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Fee, interest or finance charge`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Balance transfer or funds transfer`))'s excluded

-- cl.3.3(xii) via the exclusion list: the MCC and the description.
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 4829))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 9311))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase described as` `the base purchase` `AXS`))'s excluded
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase described as` `the base purchase` `Amaze with a transit or payment counterparty`))'s excluded

-- A bare Amaze descriptor is not on the Citi list, so it earns.
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase described as` `the base purchase` `Amaze`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 120

-- cl.3.2: a refunded purchase is not accredited.
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase later reversed` `the base purchase`))'s excluded

-- No category: a restaurant, a department store and a petrol station all earn the flat rate.
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5812))'s `units certain` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5311))'s `units certain` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5541))'s `units certain` EQUALS 120

-- No presentation: a wallet tap, a physical tap and a card number online earn alike.
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase paid by` `the base purchase` `Wallet tapped on a reader`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase paid by` `the base purchase` `Card number entered online`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase paid by` `the base purchase` `Wallet used in an app or on a website`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 120

-- Brackets. Code unknown: the floor is 0 (the code might be excluded) and the ceiling 120.
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase with unknown code` `the base purchase`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`purchase with unknown code` `the base purchase`))'s `units at best` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT elem `The merchant category code is not known` ((`PremierMiles on` (`purchase with unknown code` `the base purchase`))'s `depends on`)
-- Code 6531 sits inside the 6529-6540 heading and is not itself printed: the open reading.
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 6531))'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`PremierMiles on` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 6531))'s `units at best` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT elem `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)` ((`PremierMiles on` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 6531))'s `depends on`)
-- A settled answer names no condition.
#ASSERT null ((`PremierMiles on` `the base purchase`)'s `depends on`)

-- Miles: one Citi Mile is one mile.
#ASSERT fromMaybe 0 ((`PremierMiles on` `the base purchase`)'s `miles certain`) EQUALS 120
#ASSERT fromMaybe 0 ((`PremierMiles on` `S$100 in Malaysian ringgit`)'s `miles at best`) EQUALS 220

-- cl.3.4: the renewal bonus needs a purchase in the membership year.
#ASSERT `the renewal Citi Miles for` TRUE EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the renewal Citi Miles for` FALSE EQUALS 0
